Presentation is Flutter-only. Views observe ViewModels via `BlocBuilder`; ViewModels never import widgets.

Flow: `View → Intent → Action → Command → Cubit → UseCase`

## Command pattern

**Presentation commands** (`presentation/commands/`) are the Cubit input, dispatched by **Actions**:

- One sealed command hierarchy per screen/flow (e.g. `ItemListCommand`).
- Variants carry parameters (e.g. `FilterItemList(ItemCategory category)`).
- Actions map Intent → Command → `Cubit.execute()`.
- Cubits expose a single entry point: `execute(<Feature>Command command)`.
- Views never call `execute()` from widget callbacks — use Intents. **Exception:** initial load in `BlocProvider.create` may call `execute` once.

```dart
// presentation/commands/item_list_command.dart
sealed class ItemListCommand {
  const ItemListCommand();
}

final class LoadItemListCommand extends ItemListCommand {
  const LoadItemListCommand();
}

final class FilterItemListCommand extends ItemListCommand {
  const FilterItemListCommand(this.category);
  final ItemCategory category;
}

final class RefreshItemListCommand extends ItemListCommand {
  const RefreshItemListCommand();
}
```

## Actions, Intents & Shortcuts

Route user interactions through Flutter’s **Intent → Action** system so keyboard shortcuts can be added without changing Views or ViewModels.

| Flutter class | Location | Role |
|---------------|----------|------|
| **Intent** | `presentation/intents/` | Describes a user action. Subclass `Intent`. Key-bindable. |
| **Action** | `presentation/actions/` | Handles an Intent. Subclass `ContextAction<T>`. Maps Intent → Command → `Cubit.execute()`. |
| **Shortcuts** | Screen or app shell | Maps `LogicalKeySet` → Intent. |

Rules:

- Views call `Actions.invoke(context, const MyIntent())` — never `cubit.execute()` from widget callbacks.
- One Intent per user action; mirror Command parameters on the Intent when needed.
- Actions read the Cubit from context and dispatch the matching Command.
- Override `invoke(T intent, [BuildContext? context])` — `ContextAction` receives the context as an optional parameter and has no `context` field.
- The context is null when no invocation context is available; for shortcut-triggered actions fall back to `primaryFocus?.context`.
- Nest **`Shortcuts` as the ancestor of `Actions`** (Shortcuts above Actions in the tree).

```dart
// presentation/intents/item_list_intent.dart
final class LoadItemListIntent extends Intent {
  const LoadItemListIntent();
}

final class FilterItemListIntent extends Intent {
  const FilterItemListIntent(this.category);
  final ItemCategory category;
}

final class RefreshItemListIntent extends Intent {
  const RefreshItemListIntent();
}

// presentation/actions/item_list_action.dart
final class LoadItemListAction extends ContextAction<LoadItemListIntent> {
  @override
  void invoke(LoadItemListIntent intent, [BuildContext? context]) {
    context?.read<ItemListCubit>().execute(const LoadItemListCommand());
  }
}

final class FilterItemListAction extends ContextAction<FilterItemListIntent> {
  @override
  void invoke(FilterItemListIntent intent, [BuildContext? context]) {
    context?.read<ItemListCubit>().execute(
      FilterItemListCommand(intent.category),
    );
  }
}

final class RefreshItemListAction extends ContextAction<RefreshItemListIntent> {
  @override
  void invoke(RefreshItemListIntent intent, [BuildContext? context]) {
    // Shortcut invocations can arrive without a context.
    final targetContext = context ?? primaryFocus?.context;
    if (targetContext == null) {
      return;
    }
    targetContext.read<ItemListCubit>().execute(const RefreshItemListCommand());
  }
}
```

## Cubit for ViewModels (MVVM)

- Name cubits `*Cubit` (not `*ViewModel` or `*Bloc`).
- One Cubit per screen or cohesive UI concern.
- State is a sealed class — prefer shared `LoadState<T>` from `package:core` when it fits.
- Inject use cases via constructor; resolve with `getIt` at the composition root.
- Views are passive: Intents + emitted state only.

## Canonical vertical slice (template)

Prefer extending this pattern over inventing parallel styles. In each app’s `AGENTS.md`, replace `Item` / `catalog` with domain types.

```dart
// presentation/view_models/item_list_cubit.dart
class ItemListCubit extends Cubit<LoadState<List<Item>>> {
  ItemListCubit(this._loadItemList) : super(const LoadInitial());

  final LoadItemList _loadItemList;

  Future<void> execute(ItemListCommand command) async => switch (command) {
        LoadItemListCommand() || RefreshItemListCommand() => _load(),
        FilterItemListCommand(:final category) => _load(category: category),
      };

  Future<void> _load({ItemCategory? category}) async {
    emit(const LoadLoading());
    final result = await _loadItemList(category: category);
    emit(switch (result) {
      Right(:final value) => LoadSuccess(value),
      Left(:final value) => LoadFailure(value),
    });
  }
}

// presentation/views/item_list_screen.dart
class ItemListScreen extends StatelessWidget {
  const ItemListScreen({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return Shortcuts(
      shortcuts: {
        LogicalKeySet(LogicalKeyboardKey.keyR):
            const RefreshItemListIntent(),
      },
      child: Actions(
        actions: {
          LoadItemListIntent: LoadItemListAction(),
          FilterItemListIntent: FilterItemListAction(),
          RefreshItemListIntent: RefreshItemListAction(),
        },
        child: BlocProvider(
          create: (_) => ItemListCubit(getIt<LoadItemList>())
            ..execute(const LoadItemListCommand()),
          child: BlocBuilder<ItemListCubit, LoadState<List<Item>>>(
            builder: (context, state) => switch (state) {
              LoadSuccess() => FilledButton(
                  onPressed: () => Actions.invoke(
                    context,
                    const RefreshItemListIntent(),
                  ),
                  child: const Text('Refresh'),
                ),
              LoadFailure(:final failure) => Text(failure.message),
              LoadLoading() => const CircularProgressIndicator(),
              LoadInitial() => const SizedBox.shrink(),
            },
          ),
        ),
      ),
    );
  }
}

// ❌ BAD — widget calls Cubit directly (not key-bindable)
onPressed: () =>
    context.read<ItemListCubit>().execute(const LoadItemListCommand()),

// ✅ GOOD — widget invokes an Intent
onPressed: () => Actions.invoke(context, const RefreshItemListIntent()),

// ❌ BAD — Cubit constructs domain strategies / talks to repositories
FilterItemListCommand(:final category) => _load(
  filter: CategoryItemFilter(category),
),

// ✅ GOOD — Cubit passes data; use case owns strategy selection
FilterItemListCommand(:final category) => _load(category: category),
```
